WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.507
(soft, mysterious music)

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:07.372
- I believe that the
word cold cases is wrong,

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:09.698
because it could be
perhaps something that's

00:00:09.698 --> 00:00:12.088
in a drawer somewhere in an office,

00:00:12.088 --> 00:00:14.776
but their families hasn't forgotten them.

00:00:14.776 --> 00:00:16.880
They are still looking for them,

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.880
and I just wanna do my best to help.

00:00:23.114 --> 00:00:24.349
- [Narrator] When authorities have failed

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:26.166
to identify the remains of a body,

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:28.098
there is very little hope of closure

00:00:28.098 --> 00:00:30.405
for these John and Jane Does.

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:33.674
But every year, an enterprising
studio of student artists

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:35.647
use their knowledge of the human form

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:38.873
to try and breathe life
into these cold cases.

00:00:38.873 --> 00:00:43.239
- Here, we're doing a forensic
reconstruction of a real case,

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:46.779
trying to get it as close
as he used to look like

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:50.962
when he was alive, so we can identify him.

00:00:50.962 --> 00:00:54.198
(plucked string music)

00:00:54.198 --> 00:00:58.302
We are given a 3-D print,
not the real skull.

00:00:58.302 --> 00:01:02.446
We use it as a framework,
so we can reconstruct

00:01:02.446 --> 00:01:04.946
the anatomy of the individual.

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:09.628
First, we start adding the muscles

00:01:09.628 --> 00:01:12.429
on the framework given by the bone,

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:15.807
and then we try to complete those things

00:01:15.807 --> 00:01:19.890
that are not so clear,
like the ear or the mouth.

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:24.853
Right now, I'm working on
a Caucasian white man,

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:27.784
between 40 to 60 years old.

00:01:27.784 --> 00:01:30.467
There are indications
that he lost his teeth

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:34.634
when he was alive, and his
bones are telling me all that.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.226
- [Narrator] These lifelike
models are provided

00:01:39.226 --> 00:01:42.991
to authorities, often
reinvigorating investigations

00:01:42.991 --> 00:01:46.284
and bringing much-needed
closure to loved ones.

00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:48.650
- After my first experience last year,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.853
I was lucky enough that
the person was identified,

00:01:51.853 --> 00:01:54.450
and I got this beautiful
letter from the family members,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.033
saying "Thank you."

00:01:57.092 --> 00:02:00.497
When we see this process,
it feels almost like

00:02:00.497 --> 00:02:03.039
you're resuscitating someone.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:04.980
But I know that beyond that,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.853
what you're resuscitating is the life

00:02:06.853 --> 00:02:11.020
of those families that are
looking for this person.

